A||||3||Fformula88||4-spoke to 3-spoke steering wheel part 2||||1||
Z||000000||Fformula88||06-12-2001||10:48 PM||||I just wanted to post an update to my questions last week.  I ordered the Fiero Store's NEW leather GT style wheel.  It isn't a recovered original, but a newly manufactured one.  It is only the outer rim and needs the hub from a 3-spoke wheel.  Here's how it works...<P>Here is what I did...<BR>After removing the horn button from the old wheel (I am making the assumption the wheel is now OFF the car, and the horn button is back on it) there is a plastic dish underneath with 4 rivets holding it on.  After removing the rivets, the plastic dish comes off exposing 5 (maybe 6) torx screws which hold the wheel rim onto the hub that attaches to the column.  I just removed the old wheel rim, set my new one on the hub and re-attached the torx screws.  A couple #6 bolts replaced the rivits to hold everything back in place and I was ready to install it on the car!  So anyone without a 3-spoke who wants to get one, you will need a donor 3-spoke.<P>As for the wheel itself, it seems to be of good quality.  It feels nice without any sponginess.  All the leather is tight and stitched well.  The only part that looks a little infinished is the spoke leather where it meets the rim.  Its been glued down, but isn't quite as smooth a transition between the two pieces of leather as the original wheel.  But I don't think it will come apart either.  I love the feel, and its drives a little more sporty because its a little smaller in diameter than my 4-spok.e  Oeverall I am very pleased! <P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000001||Alex2004||06-12-2001||11:01 PM||||So would i needa swap hubs if i was going to a 4 spoke steering wheel? It would be the one with the 2 horn buttons?  My 3 spoke is bent preventing me from turning my bright's on unless i turn the wheel a certain direction so i was wanting to go w/ a 4 spoke w/ the 2 horn buttons.  Let me know!<P>Alex...<BR>PS: Glad you like your new wheel!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000002||Fformula88||06-12-2001||11:04 PM||||Nope, the 4 spoke wheels with the side horn buttons are all one peice.  Actually, any 3 spoke off a Fiero will work by itself too... its just the new wheels don't have the hubs with the.  But for your needs... just get a 4 spoke wheel, be sure the center cap and horn buttons are in good shape (I have seen two break off!) and you'll be all set!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex2004||06-14-2001||01:13 PM||||alright, thanks!<P>Alex...||||reg||6
